nforced. The same outside-root paths are rejected by guarded helpers, but these public read and write flows still use raw file APIs.  ### Details  - **Vulnerability type:** File sandbox bypass - **Affected component:** `TransitionParser.train`, `TransitionParser.parse`, `AveragedPerceptron.save`, `AveragedPerceptron.load`, `PerceptronTagger.save_to_json`, `save_maxent_params` - **Affected versions:** Published `3.9.4` and current source `v3.10.0-rc2` both reproduced. - **Patched versions:** Not yet patched - **Root cause:** Model import and export helpers use built-in `open()` on caller-controlled paths instead of pathsec-aware helpers.  `TransitionParser.train()` writes outside allowed roots, `TransitionParser.parse()` reads outside allowed roots, `AveragedPerceptron` bypasses the sandbox in both directions, and adjacent read-side helpers in the same family already show the intended guarded behavior. I confirmed outside-root reads and writes while `pathsec.open()` or the guarded sibling helpers rejected the same paths.  ### PoC  **Preconditions** - The application enables `pathsec` enforcement and lets untrusted workflows choose model import or export paths.  **Steps** 1. Enable `pathsec.ENFORCE=True` and restrict allowed roots to a dedicated sandbox directory. 2. Use public model import or export APIs with paths that point outside that root. 3. Observe the same paths are rejected by negative-control guarded helpers such as `pathsec.open()`, `PerceptronTagger.load_from_json()`, or `load_maxent_params()`. 4. Observe the vulnerable APIs still read or write outside-root files successfully.  **Minimal reproducible excerpt**  ```text transition_train_exists True transition_parse_loader_read_bytes 13 averaged_load_keys ['bias'] maxent_save wrote ['alwayson.tab', 'labels.txt'] ```  ### Impact  Consumers that rely on `pathsec` for local containment can be tricked into reading or overwriting files outside approved roots through normal model persistence and loading APIs.  ### Remediation  Route all model-path file access through `nltk.pathsec.open()` or existing pathsec-aware helpers, and add regression tests that pair each vulnerable API with a negative control on the same path."}]}, {"name": "openpyxl", "version": "3.1.5", "vulns": []}, {"name": "opentelemetry-api", "version": "1.44.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "opentelemetry-exporter-otlp", "version": "1.44.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-common", "version": "1.44.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-grpc", "version": "1.44.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-http", "version": "1.44.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "opentelemetry-proto", "version": "1.44.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "opentelemetry-sdk", "version": "1.44.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "opentelemetry-semantic-conventions", "version": "0.65b0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "orjson", "version": "3.12.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "ormsgpack", "version": "1.12.2", "vulns": []}, {"name": "packageurl-python", "version": "0.17.6", "vulns": []}, {"name": "packaging", "version": "26.3", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pathspec", "version": "1.1.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pillow", "version": "12.3.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pip", "version": "26.2.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pip-api", "version": "0.0.35", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pip-audit", "version": "2.10.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pip-requirements-parser", "version": "32.0.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "platformdirs", "version": "4.13.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "playwright", "version": "1.62.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pluggy", "version": "1.6.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "prometheus-client", "version": "0.26.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "prompt-toolkit", "version": "3.0.53", "vulns": []}, {"name": "protobuf", "version": "7.36.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "psycopg", "version": "3.3.4", "vulns": []}, {"name": "psycopg-binary", "version": "3.3.4", "vulns": []}, {"name": "psycopg-pool", "version": "3.3.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "py-s